Is $(1, 4)$ valid? $1 \le 4/2 = 2$. Yes.
Is $(2, 3)$ valid? $2 \le 3/2 = 1.5$. No.
So from $\{1, 2, 3, 4\}$, we can form pairs.
If we pair $(1, 2)$, remaining are $\{3, 4\}$. Can we pair $(3, 4)$? $3 \le 4/2 = 2$. No. So we get 1 pair.
If we pair $(1, 3)$, remaining are $\{2, 4\}$. Can we pair $(2, 4)$? $2 \le 2$. Yes. So we get 2 pairs.
So pairing smallest with smallest valid seems better? Or maybe pairing smallest with largest?
