The grid squares are defined by integer coordinates. Specifically, a square can be identified by the coordinates of its center or its vertices.
The problem statement says: "find the number of integer pairs $(i,j)$ such that all four points $(i+0.5,j+0.5), (i+0.5,j-0.5), (i-0.5,j+0.5), \text{ and } (i-0.5,j-0.5)$ are at a distance of at most $R$ from the origin."

